      "dom_id": "step-q120362",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Express $\\sqrt{2}-2\\sqrt{2}{sin}^{2}⁡{55}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      "worked_solution": "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{55}^{∘})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={55}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{55}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {55}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{110}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{55}^{∘}) & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{110}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
